Values should return multiple values.
the REPL should collect multiple values and display them:

    (setq /// // // / / (multiple-value-list (eval expr)))
    (format t "~&--> ~{~S~^ ;~%    ~}~%" /)

bocl repl:

    CL-USER> (values (type-of *standard-output*) (eq *standard-output* *trace-output*))
    
    FILE-STREAM
    CL-USER>

expected:

    CL-USER> (values (type-of *standard-output*) (eq *standard-output* *trace-output*))
    --> FILE-STREAM ;
        T
    CL-USER>


RESOLUTION (2026-07-18) — v1.8.54
---------------------------------
bocl_repl now echoes EVERY returned value, one per line (the value list
was already collected for the / history; only the echo ignored it):

    CL-USER> (values (type-of *standard-output*) (eq *standard-output* *trace-output*))
    FILE-STREAM
    NIL

Residual nit, pre-existing and out of scope here: a 0-values form —
(values) — echoes NIL instead of nothing, because a count=0 result is
normalized to one NIL somewhere in the evale call epilogue (multiple-
value propagation itself is correct: (multiple-value-list (values))
=> ()).  Cosmetic only.
